        {
          "type": "turn_end",
          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto has built three AI agents:\n\n1. **Fraud Detection Agent** (offline-evals): Reviews events and organizers on a ticketing platform, recommending approve/reject/request-info to human admins. It auto-approves only on evidence verified in code; web sources can hold decisions back but never approve. Offline evals showed significant improvements with Claude Haiku 5.5 chosen for deployment.\n\n2. **Organizer Support Agent** (coming-soon): Answers event organizers' questions about sales, payouts and setup without human review, pulling live data from PostgreSQL and the payments API.\n\n3. **Portfolio Agent** (personal-project): An agent on his portfolio site that answers visitors' questions about his experience and projects in natural language. It's also exposed as an MCP server so external agents can query it.",
            "toolCalls": [],
            "stopReason": "end_turn",
